---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="About · AI Datasets">
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p>
      Hugging Face and Papers with Code list thousands of datasets. This site goes the other way: a few
      dozen that shaped AI, each shown well enough that you come away knowing what the data looks like.
    </p>
    <h2>How entries are chosen</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>It changed the field (ImageNet, MNIST, SQuAD), or</li>
      <li>it is still used everywhere (COCO, MMLU, GSM8K), or</li>
      <li>it is in every introductory course (Iris, Titanic, CIFAR-10).</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Where the samples come from</h2>
    <p>
      At build time a script picks a fixed random sample of rows from the
      <a href="https://huggingface.co/docs/dataset-viewer">Hugging Face dataset viewer</a>.
      Samples stay under each dataset's license, which is listed on its page.
      For benchmarks whose authors ask that test items not be posted online, only sample or dev items are shown.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
<style>
  .prose { max-width: 680px; padding-top: 16px; }
</style>
